WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Alice: Good morning everyone. Let's start the sprint review for sprint twenty-three.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Alice: This sprint we focused on two main areas: the transcript ingestion service and the first pass at the extraction pipeline.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Bob: I completed the ingestion module. It now accepts VTT files and plain text transcripts. I also added basic speaker label detection. Let me do a quick demo.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Bob: The key decision we made was to normalise everything to a plain text format before analysis. This means we strip timestamps and speaker labels during the normalisation stage, which keeps the downstream AI prompt simpler.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Carol: I worked on the extraction pipeline scaffolding. We have a sequence of stages now. Each stage takes a context object and returns a modified context. It is a simple in-process pipeline for now.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Carol: We did hit one blocker this sprint. The AI model API has a token limit that affects long meetings. We are planning to chunk the transcript in a future sprint.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Alice: That is a good point. We should add a risk note. If the transcript is very long, the current approach will fail silently. We need to add validation before we ship this to production.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Bob: Agreed. One more thing I wanted to flag: we are currently using synchronous calls to the AI API. For large batches this will be slow. We may want to look at parallel execution in a later sprint.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Carol: For next sprint, I am planning to add the first real AI analysis stage. We will start with an engineering summary extraction. We also need to document the stage interface so others can contribute stages.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Alice: Great work everyone. Let's make sure those action items get logged. I will add the token limit validation to the backlog.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Alice: Thanks for joining. We will share the recording for anyone who missed it.
